  "title": "c-VEP dataset from Thielen et al. (2021)",
  "description": "This dataset contains 8-channel EEG recordings from 30 healthy participants performing a code-modulated visual evoked potential (c-VEP) brain-computer interface task. Participants fixated on target cells in a 20-symbol grid while all cells flashed with pseudo-random Gold code sequences. The data support the development of calibration-free (zero-training) BCIs using a reconvolution-based encoding model, compared against traditional ERP template matching.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded at 512 Hz from 8 Ag/AgCl electrodes (Biosemi ActiveTwo) while 30 participants completed 5 blocks of 20 trials, each 31.5 s long. Stimuli were luminance-modulated 126-bit Gold codes presented on an iPad Pro at 60 Hz in a 4x5 calculator grid. Analysis used template-matching with a reconvolution encoding model under four training regimes, with 2-30 Hz band-pass filtering and downsampling to 120 Hz.",
